    "_metadata": {
     "name": "Sidney Crosby",
     "description": "In an already illustrious career, Sidney Crosby added another remarkable achievement to his name by reaching the 1,500 career points milestone. This accomplishment solidified his place as the 15th player in the history of the game to attain such a feat. Crosby reached this milestone by scoring two goals and an assist against the Detroit Red Wings. The first goal occurred in the closing seconds of the first period, as Crosby\u2019s relentless forecheck applied pressure on Jake Walman, eventually leading to a turnover. Crosby seized the puck right in front of the net and sniped a backhand shot upstairs. After notching an assist in the second period to hit 1,499 points, Crosby reached the milestone with his second goal of the game during a Penguins power play early in the third period. Kris Letang delivered a pass, and Crosby, positioned at the top of the circle, released a perfectly placed wrist shot top shelf.\n\nOfficially Licensed Product of the NHL, NHLPA, and/or NHLAA. All copyright, logos, and marks are the property of their respective owners and are used, under license, by Sweet. All Rights Reserved. [Terms Apply](https://nhlbreakaway.com/terms).",
